.TH CCHAN_RECV 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cchan_recv \- receive a message from the cchan (it blocks)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval cchan_recv(cchan *ch, cmessage *target_buf);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Receives a message from the channel, waiting as long as it takes for
one to arrive. The queue is chosen from the thread that calls it: The
owner thread receives from the cchan_workers_to_owner queue and any
other thread receives from the cchan_owner_to_workers queue. The
message's data is handed over without a copy, so its ownership moves to
the caller.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch          Channel to receive from
target_buf  Buffer that gets the message together with the ownership
            of the data.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - A message was received. The caller must free
                     target_buf->data.
ccol_invalid_args  - ch or target_buf is NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The call blocks until a message arrives in the chosen queue. The
direction is decided from the ID of the calling thread, which is
compared with the ID of the owner that the channel took at creation.
target_buf->data belongs to the caller after a successful call, and the
caller must free it.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cchan_try_recv (3),
.BR cchan_timed_recv (3),
.BR cchan_send (3)
